  "label": "Propaganda",
  "description": "The meme uses the metaphor 'you either die a hero, or live long enough to become the villain' to frame activism as inherently risky and potentially vilifying, which is propagandistic in nature. It aims to influence viewers to reflect on the sacrifices made by activists and the potential consequences of their actions, particularly within the context of the LGBTQ+ Pride Movement. This framing can be seen as a form of propaganda that seeks to shape perception and encourage identification with the activist experience.",
